{"title":"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_(Explanation_of_Video_Solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution (Explanation of Video Solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49e6a2d706867d6652d7edadccc3fd034130bd98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> such that the following property holds: if we list the divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/4/2149f09cba97fa3185a9a26d4b3185a81a0b376a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n !$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> in increasing order as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7ce12d0865dfd5505a50984e13f541da656e9623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1=d_1&lt;d_2&lt;\\cdots&lt;d_k=n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"221\" height=\"17\" />, then we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/9/649a0a86e4f5ea5a15482e395e0c9f89c1929d03.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d_2-d_1 \\leq d_3-d_2 \\leq \\cdots \\leq d_k-d_{k-1} .\\]\" width=\"283\" height=\"15\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_.28Explanation_of_Video_Solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_(Explanation_of_Video_Solution)\">Solution (Explanation of Video Solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution (Explanation of Video Solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can start by verifying that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5635737307f5f0651cced8ee2e6558a426fd27b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39cf3e35a4981583288d2a7c4b34989916fb7360.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> work by listing out the factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/5/6859713adc973d3fbe97fafef9ce829757e54b12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3!$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/a/2da866442e69c040daf44260b4728d37e98de313.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4!$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" />. We can also see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/e/84e75ddd39b9408f4d8e7fa62d2f6cdca00232de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> does not work because the terms <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/1/781d6c823c7b7259a8ef988a562bbfe0deb724b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15, 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are consecutive factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/3/2933f407c21ceb3f3ec8370f43cd5b939250ffca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5!$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f2a6991d2108f237ee451bf37db91cacaf4134e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=6$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> does not work because the terms <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/f/d1f246b589d4808b513c6e382a0c5c5d6a1b927e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6, 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> appear consecutively in the factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/6/e26ca46a67d19ce2e5b692103305a083a2361fd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6!$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Note that if we have a prime number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/5/2758c03829033cc8a7211fc843ecb16ab0a42955.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p&gt;n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" /> and an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/d/bcd901c0c53f0132d7d5d0ebc1083ec859318466.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&gt;p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> such that both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/5/f05f085f774fc8ab50676b778b86a1f1d1114fc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> are factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, then the condition cannot be satisfied.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/6/3f665b3030352617ef67b7fb62f194fbb560fcfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is odd, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/1/211b1578ddac0afed9cde10bdf64afc2ffb36033.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)(\\frac{n-1}{2})(n-1)=n^2-2n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"258\" height=\"38\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/7/eb77020d69cb3a0a6cd7715dbe2a39b9db6d3403.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n-2)(n)=n^2-2n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"168\" height=\"21\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/3/c635138adcbbf182e1188b7c2927aad19ddc5184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n&lt;n^2-2n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/6/3f665b3030352617ef67b7fb62f194fbb560fcfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, we can use <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Bertrand%27s_Postulate\" title=\"Bertrand&#39;s Postulate\">Bertrand's Postulate</a> to show that there is at least one prime number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/8/9b89852e44a36902ba92579ed46a2c7dd7035ec5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&lt;p&lt;n^2-2n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" />. Since we have two consecutive factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and a prime number between the smaller of these factors and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, the condition will not be satisfied for all odd <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/6/3f665b3030352617ef67b7fb62f194fbb560fcfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/d/f1da611ed465b72e15d74408664e7a368fd3d307.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" /> is even, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/6/1364ab138b0a89319d39d237ac77694686046e8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)(\\frac{n-2}{2})(n-2)=n^2-4n+4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"258\" height=\"38\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/4/004c72b61817b7a7ce6e3da64db332199ccdb3e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n-3)(n-1)=n^2-4n+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"231\" height=\"21\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/0/a80e2857bae1096ab1deba7017b4f199c0595b2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n&lt;n^2-4n+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"138\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/d/f1da611ed465b72e15d74408664e7a368fd3d307.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />, we can use Bertrand's Postulate again to show that there is at least one prime number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/86626506d9f7f86c810efda28362c1cfc079d509.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&lt;p&lt;n^2-4n+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"20\" />. Since we have two consecutive factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and a prime number between the smaller of these factors and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, the condition will not be satisfied for all even <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/d/f1da611ed465b72e15d74408664e7a368fd3d307.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the only numbers that work are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5635737307f5f0651cced8ee2e6558a426fd27b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39cf3e35a4981583288d2a7c4b34989916fb7360.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>~alexanderruan\n</p><p>As listed above, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5635737307f5f0651cced8ee2e6558a426fd27b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39cf3e35a4981583288d2a7c4b34989916fb7360.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> work but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/e/84e75ddd39b9408f4d8e7fa62d2f6cdca00232de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f2a6991d2108f237ee451bf37db91cacaf4134e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=6$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> don't. Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/a/3aafb3e6e24ad13aba60fc64e72cef2815b80e29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;6$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the smallest positive integer that doesn't divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. It is easy to see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is the smallest prime greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. It is easy to see that both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/0/ab0727c08c4aaa6fa119bd3fafe17851e431fd70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/5/5d58d0cd6161c8c4be4d6284f59ec576295093e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> are divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the smallest positive integer greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> that is 2 mod 6. We see that either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/44896db1814744c051b07cbcdefe40178463efa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q=p+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/9664d4dbc8340b91bf7c61c788071c4e13f43048.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q=p+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"72\" height=\"15\" /> but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/1/111cf4cbc2306ff9a43cbf46abf1da81cedd3e12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/7/9e749d876258d86ad83071265242b4ee3fa1f502.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"15\" /> must all be divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> giving a difference of 1 after a difference of 2. Therefore, all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/a/3aafb3e6e24ad13aba60fc64e72cef2815b80e29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;6$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> fail. \n~mathophobia\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We claim only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c342b01f0cdef0f23d11a2bc9c5aa67f6d83ccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/5218af40079081e694d8b82eeac2d368ef6ea76a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> are the only two solutions. First, it is clear that both solutions work. \n</p><p>Next, we claim that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/3/67340b4f3797fad0dae6c5c0c4bd13069b662d11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &lt; 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/7/a47f57bec2b79615225569e1ab7a59d042a73c48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/cccb103143393c0119f5ab61d6d53a852ce70fcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> is not a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Let the smallest factor larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/4/c14a30af9240ebc35dbb9a357e8564d7bc2c71d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p><p>Now we consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/e/64e07b9b05a7c099e593145ff1c306b68c874980.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n!}{x-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"48\" height=\"41\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/4/aa4fb64e7dcefb840384656c299d836bcfb93fcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n!}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"39\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/c/b2c4f8554ea565cd13c79187bb5b5e2f732728b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n!}{x+k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"48\" height=\"41\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/4/1340eae0612f782d6a345574c164b1c62efc4d49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n!}{x-1} &gt; \\frac{n!}{x} &gt; \\frac{n!}{x+k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"163\" height=\"41\" />, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> were to satisfy the conditions, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/e/85e9e881b2c92c4344b4bf29b761b52910ae30e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n!}{x-1}-\\frac{n!}{x} \\geq \\frac{n!}{x} - \\frac{n!}{x+k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"203\" height=\"41\" />. However, note that this is not true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/b/44b46f646617709f9f25b41bb5014adb2884a461.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\geq 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/411e8b2b30fbb26e55ed0d28303d10fa81aa5606.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>Note that the inequality is equivalent to showing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/1/681b03296c4136842e6737ebece2e8334526cc6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{x(x-1)} \\geq \\frac{k}{x(x+k)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"167\" height=\"44\" />, which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/d/8dd6274c64b6d25c2d7837bfea4ea830a0438fca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+k \\geq kx-k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"121\" height=\"17\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/e/1ee836ffd13f21af2151e7192a174094c4ff689d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{x-2} \\geq k \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"115\" height=\"36\" />. This implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/4/b047dea407b5e9deedc73187a2888bd5ecbf45bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\geq 2x-4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/3/863c54dbe16fb785b4e4578b547435dd48b367cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\leq 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, a contradiction, since the set of numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2303664ac9f0965e10eace539666415794b052.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> are all factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, and the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must exist. Hence, no solutions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/7/a47f57bec2b79615225569e1ab7a59d042a73c48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ZcdBpaLC5p0\">https://youtu.be/ZcdBpaLC5p0</a> [video contains problem 1 and problem 4]\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO\" title=\"2024 USAMO\">2024 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2024\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted 